  "id": "hip-extension",
  "name": "Hip Extension Isolation",
  "definition": "A strict unilateral open-chain isolation movement in which the femur extends relative to a position-held pelvis while the spine and knee postures remain held. The roster owns a prone-table bent-knee fixture from 30 degrees of hip flexion to 5 degrees of extension and a standing low-pulley ankle-cuff fixture that uses two-hand machine support and extends the near-straight working leg 15 to 20 degrees behind the body. Gluteus maximus is primary and the medial hamstrings are secondary; the visible biceps-femoris region remains stabilizer-only because its unsplit mesh cannot distinguish the hip-extending long head from the monoarticular short head. Bridges, hip thrusts, hinges, quadruped kickbacks, machines, bands, unsupported cable variants, and movements driven by the pelvis or spine remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "jeon-2016-prone-table-hip-extension",
    "cybex-2008-mg500-manual"
  ],
