      "evidenceRefs": ["cybex-2008-mg500-manual", "arnold-2010-lower-limb"],
      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Attach an ankle cuff just above the working ankle to the low pulley, face the machine, and brace both hands on its pressing arm at waist height. Stand tall with a slight bend in the working knee. Log the entered stack load and compare it only on this same fixture and setup.",
        "movement": "Keep the pelvis and spine still while extending the working thigh straight behind the body.",
        "endpoint": "Stop with the working leg 15 to 20 degrees behind the body; the source reports this interval rather than one exact endpoint.",
        "returnPhase": "Bring the thigh forward under control to the neutral start without letting the stack pull the pelvis forward.",
        "controlledJoints": "Hold the slight knee bend and keep the toes and kneecap facing forward.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Use both hands for support while keeping the standing leg and trunk still.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Arching the back or rotating the pelvis changes the isolated hip action.", "Bending and straightening the working knee adds a knee-driven movement.", "Moving the cuff away from just above the ankle changes the reviewed resistance geometry."],
